    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d847">

                <pb facs="0787" n="671" xml:id="pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/307B.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 12, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>All loan agreements signed March 7. General Receiver Reed Paige Clark sails 14th
                    for Europe and expects to reach Monrovia about May 1.</p>
                <p>Negotiations with creditors in Europe will be undertaken by Mr. Robert P.
                    Skinner, American Consul General, Hamburg, as Special Representative of Falkner,
                    immediately upon Clark’s arrival in London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
